{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0129twCh9cxTFtRiJh7bmQsd","type":"tool_result","content":"599\t\\section{Conclusion}\n600\t\\label{sec:conclusion}\n601\t\n602\tWe presented a systematic token-level analysis framework for VLAs and applied it to three architectures across four task suites.\n603\tOur central finding is that VLA fine-tuning produces two architecture-independent training signatures---R$^2$ exit collapse and heightened counterfactual sensitivity---confirmed in 9 of 10 matrix cells across three VLA families.\n604\tA three-tier routing gradient reveals that instruction routing emerges at the VLM-to-VLA transition and reshapes with task specialization, with L1 attention routing inherited from the base model rather than created by fine-tuning.\n605\tThese findings provide mechanistic grounding for VLA design: entry-exit routing patterns and exit collapse diagnostics can guide architecture optimization and training monitoring.\n606\t\n607\t%% ============================================================\n608\t%%  REFERENCES\n609\t%% ============================================================\n610\t{\\small\n611\t\\bibliographystyle{plainnat}\n612\t\\begin{thebibliography}{10}\n613\t\n614\t\\bibitem{belinkov2022probing}\n615\tY.~Belinkov.\n616\t\\newblock Probing classifiers: Promises, shortcomings, and advances.\n617\t\\newblock \\emph{Computational Linguistics}, 48(1):207--219, 2022.\n618\t\n619\t\\bibitem{brohan2023rt2}\n620\tA.~Brohan \\etal\n621\t\\newblock {RT-2}: Vision-language-action models transfer web knowledge to robotic control.\n622\t\\newblock In \\emph{CoRL}, 2023.\n623\t\n624\t\\bibitem{grant2026visual}\n625\tH.~Grant \\etal\n626\t\\newblock Visual dominance in vision-language-action models.\n627\t\\newblock \\emph{arXiv preprint}, 2026.\n628\t\n629\t\\bibitem{haon2025lost}\n630\tA.~Haon \\etal\n631\t\\newblock Lost in translation: Large language models in robotics instruction following.\n632\t\\newblock In \\emph{ICRA}, 2025.\n633\t\n634\t\\bibitem{kim2024openvla}\n635\tM.~Kim \\etal\n636\t\\newblock {OpenVLA}: An open-source vision-language-action model.\n637\t\\newblock In \\emph{CoRL}, 2024.\n638\t\n639\t\\bibitem{kornblith2019similarity}\n640\tS.~Kornblith, M.~Norouzi, H.~Lee, and G.~Hinton.\n641\t\\newblock Similarity of neural network representations revisited.\n642\t\\newblock In \\emph{ICML}, 2019.\n643\t\n644\t\\bibitem{kriegeskorte2008representational}\n645\tN.~Kriegeskorte, M.~Mur, and P.~Bandettini.\n646\t\\newblock Representational similarity analysis.\n647\t\\newblock \\emph{Frontiers in Systems Neuroscience}, 2:4, 2008.\n648\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01MMLT5zPyMjm42iXmqSN4xD","session_id":"6f46fab0-1092-4dec-b5ea-345cef574fce","uuid":"b8ff7076-e624-4d71-a19f-a769959c3349","timestamp":"2026-05-22T03:15:18.223Z"}
